  "note": "Election of the Donaghadee Urban Council, nominations closed 4 September 1946. Only four nominations were received for the nine seats, so all four were returned unopposed (Belfast News-Letter, 5 September 1946, p. 3). Four returned unopposed, leaving five seats unfilled. A round-up on 6 September 1946 (p. 5) adds that three retiring councillors, Mrs. Agnew, Mr. J. M'Cullough and Mr. W. Campbell, would be re-elected automatically if they accepted, leaving two vacancies; they are recorded as deemed re-elected (seven members, two seats vacant). Returned unopposed.",
  "correctionNote": "Corrected from the page image of Belfast News-Letter, 6 September 1946, p. 5 (council-audit, Nov 2026): the three retiring councillors to be re-elected automatically under the 1946 Act (Mrs. Agnew, J. M'Cullough, W. Campbell) were added as deemed re-elected; the earlier note read this as a conflict, but four nominees plus three deemed re-elected and two vacancies make the nine seats."
